Structure Preparation and Target Residue Identification
1. 6M0J.pdb (Crystal structure of SARS-CoV-2 spike RBD bound to ACE2) was used as the initial template.
2. PyMOL was applied to visualize the RBD–ACE2 interface, identify targetable residues, and generate the spike-focused target PDB file.
3. PDFfixer was used to repair and preprocess the protein structure to ensure compatibility with downstream modeling tools.

Binder Design Pipeline
1. RFdiffusion was used to generate initial binder scaffolds against selected RBD interface residues.
2. ProteinMPNN was employed for sequence design and optimization on the RFdiffusion-generated backbones.

